# The mt7925e driver process: Linux's driver for MediaTek's MT7925 WiFi 7
# cards on PCIe (the test PC's RZ717, PCI 14C3:0717), on Linux's 802.11
# stack (stacks/wifi.manifest), added to what every driver process is built
# from (linuxdrv/emul/manifest; scripts/linux-tree.sh driver). `linux` lines:
# Linux's own objects, by path in the tree, built by Linux's make. `include`
# lines: a stack several driver processes share, under linuxdrv/.

# The driver, as Linux builds it: mt76's core, the connac and mt792x
# libraries it shares with its siblings, then mt7925's common and PCIe
# parts. (Its debugfs and trace files compile to almost nothing without
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS and tracepoints.)
